x514 text "A0: `fn NAME T... -> T`, lines `ID OP ARG...`, `ret ARG`, `end`. Types u32 bool, arrays u32x4, records (u32,bool). Params p0 p1... Args: earlier ID, pN, u32 literal, true, false. Ops exact mod 2^32.\n"
x515 puts x513 x514
x516 write x515 2
x517 text "add sub mul and or xor (bool too) shl shr (count&31) div (b=0: 4294967295) rem (b=0: a) eq ne lt le gt ge (unsigned, -> bool) select c x y\n"
x518 puts x516 x517
x519 write x518 2
x520 text "call F a... | fold F n s a... state=s; i<n: state=F(state,i,a...)\n"
x521 puts x519 x520
x522 write x521 2
x523 text "arr e... | rec e... | get a i (i mod N) | set a i v | at r k | put r k v\n"
x524 puts x522 x523
x525 write x524 2
x526 text "EDIT: reply bare edit lines, e.g. `c add a b` (replaces c or inserts before ret; `c add a b @ x` inserts after x), `-c`, `ret c`, `fn f ...` (adds/replaces a function), `-fn f`.\n"
x527 puts x525 x526
x528 call close x527 
x529 call close x528 
x530 call close x529 
x531 call open x530 13
x532 write x531 4
x533 write x532 1
x534 text "programs"
x535 puts x533 x534
x536 call open x535 11
x537 write x536 2
x538 text "Programs and functions"
x539 puts x537 x538
x540 call close x539 
x541 call open x540 2
x542 write x541 2
x543 text "A program is a list of functions. A function is a header `fn NAME T... -> T`, then one instruction per line `ID OP ARGS`, then `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`, which names a fresh node), then `end`. Names are lowercase identifiers. Parameters are p0, p1, ... in header order. An argument is an earlier ID in the same function, a parameter, a u32 literal, true, or false. There are no forward references, no recursion, and no nested expressions."
x544 puts x542 x543
x545 call close x544 
x546 call open x545 10
x547 write x546 4
x548 write x547 2
x549 text "code"
x550 puts x548 x549
x551 call open x550 4
x552 call open x551 6
x553 write x552 4
x554 write x553 2
x555 text "cm"
x556 puts x554 x555
x557 write x556 2
x558 text "# clamp p0 into [p1, p2]\n"
x559 puts x557 x558
x560 call close x559 
x561 write x560 2
x562 text "fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\nend"
x563 puts x561 x562
x564 call close x563 
x565 call close x564 
x566 call close x565 
x567 call open x566 13
x568 write x567 4
x569 write x568 1
x570 text "types"
x571 puts x569 x570
x572 call open x571 11
x573 write x572 2
x574 text "Types and values"
x575 puts x573 x574
x576 call close x575 
x577 call open x576 2
x578 write x577 2
x579 text "u32 is an exact 32-bit unsigned integer; every arithmetic result wraps modulo 2^32. bool is true or false, never a number. Arrays u32xN and records (T,T,...) are values: get, set, at, and put return a copy, they never alias. io is a linear token, meaning every io value is used exactly once; that is what makes output order checkable."
x580 puts x578 x579
x581 call close x580 
x582 call close x581 
x583 call open x582 13
x584 write x583 4
x585 write x584 1
x586 text "iteration"
x587 puts x585 x586
x588 call open x587 11
x589 write x588 2
x590 text "Iteration"
x591 puts x589 x590
x592 call close x591 
x593 call open x592 2
x594 write x593 2
x595 text "A function body has no loops. Repetition is fold and loop over an earlier function: the step function receives the state, the index, and any extra arguments, and returns the next state. loop adds a predicate function that is checked before each iteration. A literal count is checked against a per-function budget when the program is checked. A variable count is bounded by fuel (a step budget) in the reference interpreter, the plain slow implementation that every target is compared with; compiled targets have no execution budget."
x596 puts x594 x595
x597 call close x596 
x598 call open x597 10
x599 write x598 4
x600 write x599 2
x601 text "code"
x602 puts x600 x601
x603 call open x602 4
x604 call open x603 6
x605 write x604 4
x606 write x605 2
x607 text "cm"
x608 puts x606 x607
x609 write x608 2
x610 text "# sum of squares 0..n-1 with fold; the step is an earlier function\n"
x611 puts x609 x610
