x653 write x652 2
x654 text "Views and edits"
x655 puts x653 x654
x656 call close x655 
x657 call open x656 2
x658 write x657 2
x659 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0), one signature line per callee, and a program handle (g0). The program view is scoped to the target, its transitive callees and its direct callers, so it stays the same size as the program grows. The revision is a short hash of the program text; an edit written against an older revision is rejected rather than applied to code that has moved. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line, as in the quick start."
